WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.000
Muscle, Tag Team Match, Team up for a rough and tumble match!

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:27.360
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.320
I'm Mike.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.860
I'm Joe. I'm Sean.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.000
And I'm Sam. Guys, how we doing?

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.600
Excellent, Michael, thank you.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.520
Great. I just wanted to make sure Sean was still alive.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.360
I'm here. Good. Sean is here.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:50.640
His soul has not been crushed yet, but maybe Muscle, M-U-S-C-L-E, otherwise known for standing for the most unusually small creatures lurking everywhere.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.940
No. Is that really what it stands for?

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.540
Yes, it is. This game's better.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.800
Usually small creatures lurking everywhere.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.220
So they're canonically small.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.740
Yes. Because they are.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:07.120
No, they're actually, but they are canonically gigantic strong men because they come from a manga.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:14.380
A, like, 13 year long manga called Kiddy Koomin, I think, or something like that.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:15.960
But they're not small on that.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.180
Yeah. They're not small there, but when did they get small?

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.680
When they came to America, they only came as little figurines.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.060
Yeah, little, like, eraser guys.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:26.580
Yeah, I guess they're just erasers.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.380
We're glossing over the fact that they're also not lurking everywhere.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:30.720
There's like six of them.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.500
They're like, alright, we got L-E in the end that we gotta figure out.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.180
So everyone is talking right now.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.640
Let's get a little more focused for a second.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:55.280
So I know I was trying to drop a bombshell there, but I'm sure some people at home who clicked on the play episode for this and have played this game before know that it came from a very famous Japanese manga anime series that also came to America during, it was on Foxbox, if anybody remembers that.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:03.440
For Kids Entertainment, the same people that licensed, like, Pokemon over to America, they bought this and said, hey, this'll, kids will love this.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:09.100
And so they brought that over and it even was on Cartoon Network and Toonami, remember, with Tom?

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.660
Oh, wow. Tom from Toonami.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:21.320
And it was on there and it's basically like a show where a bunch of different guys wrestle each other and they're all wrestling for, you know, probably some belt or something.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.000
I didn't want to go too deep in.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.820
I watched an episode of the show.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.760
It was, it was interesting.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:39.880
It's kind of like, it's like a mix between Dragon Ball Z and like something, something, I don't know, like something really funny and loose, like Looney Tunes.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.960
You know, it's like a mix between those two.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:46.380
Okay. Where there's gags and there's, and it's not that, and yeah, it doesn't take itself that seriously.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.120
There is gas involved.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.800
Goofs and gaffs. Yeah, did you, wait, did you mean gas?

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:54.760
I said gaffs. Yeah, one of them, gaffs is like one of them actually attacks by like farting.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.360
Wow. Yeah. Very, very mature, Michael.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:58.960
Well, it's not me.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.020
It's the Japanese making the games.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:05.760
Speaking of making the games, this is another Bandai Toes Tose game.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:10.240
So Bandai takes all the credit and Tose says, hey, we're in the corner over here.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:11.480
We might've made that game.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.380
Yeah, we might've made that whole game.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:26.420
So, Muscle, if you guys remember about like two weeks ago, we played tag team wrestling.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.940
Is this better, Joe?

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.640
Well, all right, let me give you my initial reaction.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:41.540
My initial reaction was that I was optimistic because literally seconds before I started playing it, I had finished playing tag team wrestling.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.500
And I was like, oh, this game's better.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:53.360
But then I also, minutes after I played tag team wrestling, I got a paper cut and I was like, oh, this paper cut's great compared to tag team wrestling.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:56.300
So it's, I was optimistic.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.060
I was like, oh, like, I feel like I'm controlling things.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:03:59.760
Looks like there's a few other moves you can do.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.560
And overall, that kind of fell flat.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:09.260
Like it was better than tag team wrestling, but I think that trips a lot of people up.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:11.340
Right. Like, right. Like it is better than tag team wrestling.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:13.220
That doesn't mean it's, it's even a good game.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:18.660
Right. There's not, you don't, you know, when the bar is so low, right, it doesn't matter.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.200
It doesn't mean that this is good.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.900
It just means that this is acceptable.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:24.120
I wouldn't even say it's acceptable.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.640
Thank you, Sean, for chiming in.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:34.080
What do you got? This, I mean, this game plays better than tag team, as we keep saying, only in that it plays at all.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:41.540
Um, you have a modicum of control over your character, as in the previous game that we played.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.380
We felt like we hardly controlled the character.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:59.340
Um, and it feels a little bit more fair, even though, uh, within this game, really the only way to win is to wait for a random power up to find, to find its way onto the screen and then to jump up and grab that.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:07.540
And I mean, it is possible to just through a war of attrition, beat your opponent, but it's really just waiting for that power up.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:18.920
Yeah. I think, I think that's the biggest issue I have with it was that, I mean, you can wail on each other as much as you can, but whoever gets the power up the most just wins.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:22.800
Yeah, but in a way, the power up is kind of like the steel chair.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:27.540
Sure. You know, it's like, it's like all of a sudden the steel chair has come out and.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:28.440
It's the smash ball.

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:36.640
That was one thing we didn't talk about in tag team wrestling, because I'm sure nobody got to it, but there is an opportunity for a steel chair to show outside.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.400
Oh yeah. It was used on me over and over.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:44.320
This is not a tag team wrestling, uh, episode though, even though this is also a tag team game.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:47.220
But I just, I just had to mention that real fast.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:52.160
One thing about the objective of this game that makes it different than tag team wrestling is that you don't pin.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.120
It's just based on like energy.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:58.020
Yeah. Energy. So you want to get them down to zero and like, and I like how it kind of shifts.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:06.580
So it's not like you each start with five energy balls and like you could be down to two, but if you start doing a lot of like good stuff, you gain them back.

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:10.340
So it is kind of more of like a tug of war than just like a, I'm out.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:11.420
I got beat up early.

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:12.840
So now I'm like out of this fight.

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:18.140
And I thought it was kind of cool with the energy that, uh, that it was actually like organically in the scene.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:21.140
It wasn't like a, it wasn't like a health bar at the top of your screen.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.040
It was like on a scoreboard in the scene.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.300
That would like, right.

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:25.240
Right. That is cool.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:31.400
The thing that bugged me about the energy is if once you get down to one, you really can't do anything and you can't go back to your corner.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:32.840
Your guy is like really slow.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:37.440
You can't jump and you can't go back to your corner fast enough to tag your, tag your teammate.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:39.120
Don't you think that's kind of cool though?

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.300
It's cool. Like stamina into the game as a thought.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:48.460
I would, I would say that cool is overstatement, but yeah, it's like, it's cool, but it's frustrating.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:51.800
Cause it's like, Oh, well I'm not dead, but I'm about to be dead.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:54.440
Right. And these guys are supposed to be like superheroes.

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:57.800
So it is kind of weird that they're like, yeah, so easily defeated.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:00.780
But I think we do need to, because we didn't really talk about it too much.

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.300
We got to talk about that combat guys.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:08.340
I mean, this time we're not hitting a punch and then pressing B, uh, like seven times to get to the good moves.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:11.200
There's some pretty cool stuff that's going on in terms of attacks.

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:19.180
We got, if you go from behind and attack them, you'll do like a little suplex, throw them over and you can do a bouncing off the ropes.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.060
That was my go to.

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:22.400
I found, Oh, go ahead.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:35.180
Thanks. I found that the easiest way to get someone was to wait for them to kind of start swinging at you, lure them over to the corner as they're like right after they swing, jump into it and then just wail them, you know?

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:37.380
Yeah. Cause you cover the most ground that way also.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:43.560
Cause I feel, I felt like even though the controllers, the controls were kind of tight, I wouldn't say super tight.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:47.220
Uh, no, they were, yeah, they definitely weren't the best.

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:52.500
Yeah. But I mean, I could, it, they made sense and you can move relatively fast enough.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:56.720
Uh, you still don't have a pretty, like you don't have a good reach.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:00.680
No. Um, and also bounce off stuff a lot.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.600
The lack of sprites.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:08.480
Um, really you can only look in two directions, even if you're moving up and down.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.820
Yeah. You're always just going to be facing left or right.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:13.960
So I don't even know if you can engage with each other.

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:16.340
If you try to attack from the top or bottom, you cannot.

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:20.000
I can confirm that you cannot, you have to attack from the side.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:21.880
Yeah. And that, that, that is pretty jank.

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:27.660
Yeah. Um, but if there's one thing I'll say in defense of that, it's that I'm not sure.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:34.700
I think that like having an up and down attack as well, like, like a way to attack that way would

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:37.660
have just complicated this game a little more than it was worth doing.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:43.700
So in that case though, why would you even introduce the ability to move in that second dimension?

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:45.880
Why don't you just move back and forth?

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:47.260
I guess to, I guess for avoiding.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.380
To avoiding and to try and get the power up first.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:55.080
I liked, I liked the ability to avoid because if they get that power ball, you only, your

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:59.420
only option is to run because the other character just goes insane.

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:04.200
And I, that was probably my favorite part of the game was getting the power ball and trying

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:07.280
out with each character, seeing like what crazy moves they do.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:08.480
One guy like throws hammers.

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:10.440
Yeah. You know, or like tomahawks.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:11.780
Yeah. Like tomahawks.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:16.420
Another one will just like be able to like reach really far over and attack.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:21.600
And then like, there was one that I did that like, he like threw the guy up in the air

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:23.460
and like pile drive them down.

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:27.580
I thought that was pretty cool that they programmed like different moves for each character.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.020
Because it was really just the special moves that had like a wide variety.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:33.560
There were some differences in the regular moves, like the jump.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:34.540
But nothing really notable.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:39.940
Yeah. Which I think was a big miss on like the, having all these unique characters and having really

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:41.460
only one difference between each other.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:46.340
Especially, yeah. Especially if like these characters are part of a manga where like their personalities matter

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:48.260
and they're all like well-known characters.

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:52.080
